11
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:56,000
Meet the Feebles (also known as Frogs of War in New Zealand as the film's English fake working title) is a 1989 New Zealand adult puppet musical black comedy film directed
by Peter Jackson, and written by Jackson, Fran Walsh, Stephen Sinclair, and Danny Mulheron (who also performed the body of lead character Heidi the Hippo).

12
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The plot follows a stage troupe of anthropomorphic
animals in a perverse comic satire.

13
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:16,000
In contrast to the positive innocence and naïve folly of The Muppets, the Feebles
largely present negativity, vice, and other misanthropic characteristics.

14
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:26,000
The film is the first Jackson co-wrote with his future partner Fran Walsh,
with the two collaborating on all his subsequent films.

15
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
The film also marked the beginning of Jackson's collaborations with Richard Taylor and Wētā Workshop,
as created by Taylor and Tania Rodger, who all worked on Jackson's subsequent films.

16
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The film explores themes of pornography, sexual abuse,
drug addiction, musical, celebrity.

17
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:56,000
The tone is lighthearted.
